      "a": "2",
      "e": "Invertibility is equivalent to: only the trivial solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$, RREF equal to $I_{n}$, a unique solution of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ for every $\\mathbf{b}$, and $\\det(A)\\neq0$. Infinitely many solutions of $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ means $A$ is <u>not</u> invertible."
